    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this",
      "id": 15,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**API-equivalent cost is a floor, not a bill.** It prices vLLM's token counters (gpt-oss-20b on the DGX Spark) at each provider's rates, from the `spark-llm` recording rules in flux-talos (`kube-prometheus-stack/app/prometheusrule-spark-llm.yaml`, where the prices live). It excludes vision (Ollama), STT and TTS, and loses any hour Prometheus missed.\n\n**Quality is not equal.** gpt-oss-20b is weaker than Sonnet or Haiku; the fair comparison is what you would otherwise have paid for output you'd accept. Free tokens also get used more freely than metered ones.\n\n**History:** raw data is kept 14 days, 1h downsamples 60 days. Ranges past 14 days rely on Thanos downsampled reads (flux-talos #2018). Cost panels are hourly samples, so pick ranges of a day or more."
      }
    }
